{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"id\":42738,\"title\":\"Duck Dynasty\",\"tagline\":\"\",\"overview\":\"At first glance the Robertsons look like a typical Louisiana family who lives for duck hunting season. A closer look, however, reveals they live very well because of duck hunting season. The Robertsons own and operate Duck Commanders, which specializes in fabricating duck calls and decoys out of salvaged swamp wood. The company has grown from a mom-and-pop operation to a multimillionaire sporting empire, established in 1973 by family patriarch Phil (aka the Duck Commander) and now run by his business-savvy son, Willie. \\\"Duck Dynasty\\\" follows the Robertsons and their booming business, which also employs Willie's wife, Korie, his brother Jase and Uncle Si, a Vietnam vet and colorful character who keeps the guys in the workshop occupied with his many stories.\",\"posterPath\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/jTXJFP9E9jo5SsGbhFs5L3WWUNX.jpg\",\"backdropPath\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/wHzAEm93xEQ3UOGThif9GqfSOnW.jpg\",\"youtubeBackdrop\":null,\"anilistBanner\":null,\"rating\":6.4,\"voteCount\":112,\"year\":2012,\"genres\":[\"Reality\",\"Comedy\"],\"status\":\"Canceled\",\"type\":\"tv\",\"totalSeasons\":11,\"totalEpisodes\":131,\"createdBy\":[],\"networks\":[\"A&E\"],\"countries\":[{\"code\":\"US\",\"name\":\"United States of America\"}],\"lastAirDate\":\"2017-04-05\",\"cast\":[{\"id\":1003836,\"name\":\"Willie Robertson\",\"character\":\"Self\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/jjJVGymVWKyiVKlEOxpAKxOs62M.jpg\"},{\"id\":1003840,\"name\":\"Korie Robertson\",\"character\":\"Self\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/1NEGmy6kwLhVhO214qlz6YMklG0.jpg\"},{\"id\":1003838,\"name\":\"Jase Robertson\",\"character\":\"Self\",\"photo\":null},{\"id\":1120364,\"name\":\"Kay Robertson\",\"character\":\"Self\",\"photo\":null},{\"id\":1003841,\"name\":\"Si Robertson\",\"character\":\"Self\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/fIXOOPOzJdmsyGSRHsXEYDW8to3.jpg\"},{\"id\":1290054,\"name\":\"Phil Robertson\",\"character\":\"Self\",\"photo\":null}],\"trailers\":[{\"key\":\"Kb_XwjnXeYA\",\"name\":\"Duck Dynasty Plan Bee Compilation\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"}],\"similar\":[{\"id\":276083,\"title\":\"Crap Happens\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/9AG5nhecHFpFShhhaHEUEnjNrgW.jpg\",\"rating\":5.9,\"year\":2026,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.21250000000000002,\"_genreOverlap\":1}],\"seasonNumber\":4,\"seasonName\":\"Season 4\",\"seasonOverview\":\"Hold on to your hunting hats! The Robertsons are back in Season 4 of  Duck Dynasty and they’ve have never had so much Southern charm.\\r\\nThis season, it's a family affair as everyone comes together to throw a surprise vow renewal for Phil and Kay. And when the guys and their wives realize Martin is foregoing poker for a date, they all take turns coaching him for romance. Meanwhile, Phil tries to teach his granddaughters how to fish, but the girls outsmart him and have him doing all the work. Later, he and Kay teach Sadie and John Luke how to make Mayhaw jelly. Th guy's antics continue as they attempt to make duck jerky, and a series of \\\"gentleman's bets\\\" leads them to the ultimate challenge of helping Phil get a wheelbarrow down from a tree.\",\"seasonPoster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/qt5XHaOBe8t83f7GXdm2cuuPVpa.jpg\",\"seasonAirDate\":\"2013-08-14\",\"episodes\":[{\"number\":1,\"name\":\"Till Duck Do Us Part\",\"overview\":\"Everyone comes together to plan a surprise wedding for Phil and Kay, setting up a special ceremony on their land, which the whole family attends. Si distracts Phil and Kay by taking them on a \\\"trip down memory lane\\\" to different places that were meaningful in their relationship.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/cBG57HCkAiMoBmecYSeE0sm87LO.jpg\",\"rating\":5,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"2013-08-14\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"So You Think You Can Date?\",\"overview\":\"After discovering that Martin has to miss a Friday night poker game for a planned date, the guys (as well as their wives) take turns figuring out the best way to coach him for romance. When babysitting for Jep and Jessica turns into a rocky road, Phil tries to teach his granddaughters how to fish--a useful skill. But even at this young age, the girls outsmart him and have him doing all the work.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/9aQurYMWzvMNgLqIx81gEumFIcW.jpg\",\"rating\":6,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"2013-08-21\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"Hot Tub Grime Machine\",\"overview\":\"The guys realize that Godwin has never really asked them for a favor, even though they are all always helping each other out. Godwin asks them to help him get a hot tub, so they set out to help him pick one up. Phil and Kay teach Sadie and John Luke how to make May Haw jelly.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ZiV4ru8H0dWzmLaY0PkPfgD0WT.jpg\",\"rating\":6,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"2013-08-28\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"A-Jase-ent Living\",\"overview\":\"Due to construction at Jase and Missy's house, Willie and Korie invite Jase and the kids to live with them while Missy is out of town visiting friends. What seems like a good gesture of Willie and Korie's part turns into conflict between two brothers due to a lack of personal space. Then, what begins in the duck call room as a series of \\\"Gentlemen's Bets,\\\" turns into a series of bets outside the Duck Call Room as well, eventually leading them to the ultimate challenge at Phil and Kay's house--helping Phil get a wheelbarrow down from a tree.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/dKCjZajlrJJGZVEZZqItNDAYaEQ.jpg\",\"rating\":6,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"2013-09-04\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"Termite be a Problem\",\"overview\":\"Because of a termite problem at Duck Commander, the guys are forced to find a different location to work from--Godwin's House. But while at Godwin's house, Godwin gets a taxidermied gift from a past relative, which sends them on a mission to find out how much it is worth. Miss Kay needs help with her Golden 60's club, so she enlists Korie and Willie to help her out.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/fnP8s1cCjjBAoulpdaw8oPVuAiF.jpg\",\"rating\":6,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"2013-09-11\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"John Luke After Dentist\",\"overview\":\"John Luke and Sadie are getting some dental work done, complete with sedation, and it's up to Willie and Korie to take care of them through the process--including getting them back home safely. Phil goes to DC to recruit Jase and Jep to help him take care of a cottonmouth den and finds them emptying the contents of the broken fridge into trash bags. They set out to dump the trash but keep running into problems.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/x9j5MzFT6v5erBI4itAVMOvzoPp.jpg\",\"rating\":5,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"2013-09-18\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"Scoot Along Si\",\"overview\":\"Si shows up to work on a mobility scooter, claiming to have an invisible injury from a fender bender with Willie. After losing her beloved turtle \\\"Mr. T\\\", Ms.Kay enlists Phil on a mission to find a new pet turtle.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/7wo2kUV2sI6HRM5NQbeqb7g7251.jpg\",\"rating\":5,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"2013-10-02\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":8,\"name\":\"Jerky Boys\",\"overview\":\"A decision to try and make some duck jerky leads the boys to Godwin's garage and a minibike race. Phil and Kay have made Willie the executor of their will, and Phil wants to show Willie what he and his brothers will inherit when he and Kay pass away.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/g0ZSLtKwLHyro8FhG1iDHul719e.jpg\",\"rating\":5,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"2013-10-09\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":9,\"name\":\"Going Si-ral\",\"overview\":\"Si discovers Youtube, and, after watching a series of instructional videos, decides he can make something better. Jase, Jep, Godwin, and Martin help Si shoot an instructional golf video, and upload Si's \\\"four point philosophy\\\" to the web. John Luke totals Willie's truck, and Willie realizes he may be raising the two worst drivers in all of Louisiana. Willie then remembers that all kids are trouble when he takes his niece and nephew for a ride in his loaner, a 2014 Chevy Silverado, and they cover it in ice cream.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/3SIyP6F8f7IR8kyrh9dngqxMN4I.jpg\",\"rating\":5,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"2013-10-16\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":10,\"name\":\"Quack O'Lanterns\",\"overview\":\"The Robertsons host a Halloween event at Duck Commander, where they all come together to transform the warehouse into a \\\"scarehouse.\\\" Everyone dresses up and Willie desperately tries to be the scariest, but none of the kids are afraid of him. The youngest grandkids help Kay make treats while Phil puts his own twist on Halloween decorating by making a jack-o-lantern with a shotgun.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ajs5qmnuy0iH5D8OvAP5ItmY4IP.jpg\",\"rating\":5,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"2013-10-23\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":11,\"name\":\"O Little Town of West Monroe\",\"overview\":\"The Robertsons perform a live nativity for their Church for Christmas, so the wives organize rehearsals to ensure that they pull off a great event. However, rehearsals get off to a bumpy start as the guys can't stop sharing their opinions. In between rehearsals, Willie and Jase struggle to get their wives the perfect Christmas gifts and they unenthusiastically take Jep's advice.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/4dwVyUelVfb4oIMgjNXqv77P1zC.jpg\",\"rating\":5,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"2013-12-11\",\"runtime\":43}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2012-03-21\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}